hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1169","Ali bin Khashram told us, Issa, meaning Ibn Yunus, told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Zurara bin Awfa, on the authority of Saad bin Hisham, on the authority of Aisha, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “whenever he prayed a prayer he would remain constant in it, and if he slept during the night or He fell ill and prayed twelve rak'ahs during the day."
"1170","Bundar narrated to us, Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, H., and Bundar narrated to us, also Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, both of them, on the authority of Saeed, H., narrated to us Bundar, also Muadh bin Hisham, my father told me both, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Zurara bin Awfa, on the authority of Saad bin Hisham, that Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “when he prayed a prayer he liked to do it constantly, and when it occupied him from praying the night prayers, Sleep, illness, or pain, he prayed twelve rak’ahs during the day.” This is the hadith of Yahya bin Saeed"
